From aa82b582c9389b85e1be3bbf55161a8d2cf1f77a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] video: Crop FMVs - letterbox-band removal at pixel aspect,
 toggle in launcher/F1/settings

fmv_crop becomes a toggle (settings.toml `fmv_crop = true|false`; older
0/8/12/16 row counts still parse, any non-zero = on). On, the GL FMV present
detects the pure-black letterbox rows a 24-bit movie carries inside its own
frame (GT2's Polyphony logo: 24 top/bottom, the intro: 28) and drops them
together with an 8-row CRT overscan trim, then fits the remaining picture at
the aspect it would have on a 4:3 CRT with those rows cut off - pixel aspect
preserved, so a widescreen movie fills the height of a 16:9 window with
narrow pillars at any resolution instead of a 4:3 rect with black bands
inside it. Detection is stable by construction (symmetric min(top,bottom),
frames without a picture in the outer quarter rejected, min over the last 60
accepted frames, history cleared between movies). Applies to every 24-bit
frame (main.cpp marks the present with gl_renderer_set_present_fmv), pinned
4:3 or not; letterbox_rect_aspect does its products in 64-bit.
